# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14, backlog K027); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: Mail is left hanging well over the right edge of the screen, as people leave windows. Safari docks
# on the right, under Mail: Mail was on the Desktop with all that showed of it, so it makes way.
# (That it is not pulled in while nothing needs its place is in FloatingWindowTests: no `expect` form says it.)
# Reference: T03 T08.
# Floating windows make way here, as they did until Q20 (collab/QUESTIONS.md); as Arbor ships they keep their frames (scenario 67).
set floatingWindowsMakeWay true
open Safari
open Mail 600x400
move 102 1000 300 600 400
dock 101 left
expect left-of 101 102
expect visible 102
float-all
dock 101 right
expect left-of 102 101
expect visible 102
